WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.925
Welcome to our training on shipping settings automation, also known as SSA.

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:08.208
Customers like purchasing products with quick delivery times.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:13.544
If you fulfill your own orders, offering accurate delivery promises can be difficult.

00:00:13.544 --> 00:00:20.110
To achieve this, you'll have to estimate how long carriers take to deliver to different regions

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.393
by keeping track of each carrier's delivery performance.

00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:29.139
When customers shop in the Amazon store, they see the delivery promise you set.

00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:29.960
On average,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.806
sellers overestimate the number of days shipping will take by 53%, resulting in unnecessarily long

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:37.260
delivery

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.228
promises that are less appealing to customers.

00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:43.620
With SSA, you can provide more accurate delivery

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:49.544
promises while eliminating the need to manually estimate transit times to different regions.

00:00:49.544 --> 00:00:50.000
This

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.800
training will cover how SSA works and how to enable SSA on your new and existing shipping templates.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:03.100
SSA provides more accurate delivery promises that are automatically calculated based on your

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.629
warehouse locations, each customer's location, and the carriers you use.

00:01:07.629 --> 00:01:09.440
Here's how it works.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.200
First, you'll select your warehouse addresses and which shipping services you use.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:15.680
Then,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.166
you'll assign your seller-fulfilled ASINs to your SSA-enabled shipping template.

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:22.080
Amazon then

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.240
auto-calculates your optimized transit times and continues to refresh carrier data to ensure

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.779
these times are always up to date.

00:01:30.779 --> 00:01:33.680
Customers will see your accurate delivery promise on

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.480
your product detail page, improving the likelihood of a purchase.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.760
Once a purchase is made, you'll

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.570
ship the order using the shipping services enabled in your SSA's shipping template.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.680
And once your

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.200
order is in transit, you'll have peace of mind knowing your shipment will arrive to the customer

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.487
closer to the promised delivery date.

00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:57.680
To enable SSA on your shipping templates, sign in to Seller

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.155
Central.

00:01:58.155 --> 00:02:02.427
Hover over the Settings icon and select Shipping Settings.

00:02:02.427 --> 00:02:04.800
On the Shipping Templates page,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:10.058
create a new shipping template or edit an existing one to activate SSA.

00:02:10.058 --> 00:02:12.080
To create a new shipping

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.275
template with SSA-enabled, select Create New Shipping Template and click OK.

00:02:17.275 --> 00:02:19.440
A pop-up window will

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.240
appear where you'll select your warehouse location.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.440
The locations you select will indicate where the

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.240
SKUs linked to this shipping template will be shipped from.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.520
Once selected, click Next to proceed

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.097
to your fulfillment preferences.

00:02:33.097 --> 00:02:37.040
On this step, you'll indicate your carrier preferences and select

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.496
the shipping services you use to fulfill orders.

00:02:40.496 --> 00:02:43.520
Finally, review your selections and click Confirm

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.160
to finish.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.280
You'll then be directed to the Create a New Shipping Template page where you can review

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.267
and edit your shipping options, regions, and rates.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.880
Review this information and if everything is

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.226
correct, click Save at the bottom of the page.

00:02:58.226 --> 00:03:01.200
Once your template is saved, begin assigning your

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.630
ASINs to your newly created SSA template.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:08.550
To do this, visit the Manage Inventory page.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.040
Here,

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.804
select the ASINs you'd like to add to your shipping template.

00:03:12.804 --> 00:03:15.200
Once selected, click the Edit drop-down

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.440
and select Change Shipping Template.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.920
To enable SSA on an existing shipping template, select the

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.595
template name you'd like to edit on the Shipping Templates page.

00:03:26.595 --> 00:03:28.720
Once selected, click Edit Template

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.100
and follow the same steps provided for creating a new shipping template.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.560
For more information on

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.189
SSA, search for Shipping Settings Automation in Seller Central.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:41.760
This concludes our SSA training.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.040
You now have the tools to enable SSA on your shipping templates and to provide quicker,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.400
more accurate delivery promises for customers.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.440
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
